  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1663\">\n<p data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1534\"><strong data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1484\">Low levels</strong> of one or more subclasses may be associated with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1663\">\n<li data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1581\">\n<p data-start=\"1539\" data-end=\"1581\">Recurrent infections (e.g., sinopulmonary)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1625\">\n<p data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1625\">Common Variable Immunodeficiency (CVID)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1628\" data-end=\"1663\">\n<p data-start=\"1630\" data-end=\"1663\">Selective IgG subclass deficiency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1664\" data-end=\"1790\">\n<p data-start=\"1666\" data-end=\"1707\"><strong data-start=\"1666\" data-end=\"1683\">Elevated IgG4</strong> may be associated with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1710\" data-end=\"1790\">\n<li data-start=\"1710\" data-end=\"1742\">\n<p data-start=\"1712\" data-end=\"1742\">IgG4-Related Disease (IgG4-RD)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1745\" data-end=\"1790\">\n<p data-start=\"1747\" data-end=\"1790\">Allergic conditions or chronic inflammation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
